# 13-ORG / organic and content

**Goes here.** Everything distributed without paying for placement. Posting cadence and
volume, format-native structure, short-form organic, community building, founder-led
content, UGC sourcing, creator and influencer collaboration, whitelisting and usage
rights, content marketing and long form, newsletters as a content product,
distribution planning, and measuring organic when there is no per-asset cost.

## Not here

- The same format running as a paid ad -> 10-MCR
- Email and SMS flows, deliverability, list mechanics -> 14-EML
- Content written to rank for a query -> 15-SEO
- What the brand stands for, positioning, brand psychology -> 04-BRD
- A single organic stunt built to be screenshotted -> 19-WLD

**The ORG and BRD line is the one that keeps breaking.** 3 brand-psychology sources
were filed here and had to move. What the brand means is BRD. How you get it in front
of people without paying is ORG.

**The ORG and EML line.** What to say and how to grow the audience is ORG. Sending
infrastructure and flow logic is EML.

**The ORG and SEO line.** A brief targeting a search query is SEO. A brief for a
newsletter or a social series is ORG.

